Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:59:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 533/533] [MoE] A modular kernel's output never lives in the
 workspace arena

The layer's output outlives the call, while the arena's views are valid
only until the next lease. With a prepared (routed/shared) workspace the
output was workspace[2]; at TP1, where no all-reduce copies it, DeepSeek
V4.1's next mHC entry leased its scratch from the same bytes and overwrote
the routed output while reading it: NaN gate logits once a batch held three
or more requests (silently wrong rows below that).
